{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Post-only order would cross the order book at 0.00007828 and was rejected. Reprice outside the touch and resubmit.",
  "code": "POST_ONLY_WOULD_CROSS"
}

// Price protection (HTTP 400): a limit SELL below 0.2x, or a limit BUY above 5x, the
// market price (median of the pair's last 20 trades in 24 h; only checked when the pair
// has at least 10 trades in that window) is refused before anything is placed. Sells
// above and buys below the market are never refused. Market orders are not affected.
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Sell price 8 USDC is far below the market price (about 800.10 USDC). Sells below 160.02 USDC are refused to protect you from a typo. Check the price and resubmit.",
  "code": "PRICE_OUT_OF_BAND",
  "band": { "sellMin": 0.2, "buyMax": 5, "reference": 800.1, "referenceSource": "median of last 20 trades", "limit": 160.02 }
}

// WHERE A POST-ONLY ORDER IS ALLOWED TO REST
//
// There are TWO venues to stay clear of, not one. Each has a threshold per
// side, and the price must be STRICTLY inside it: exactly AT a threshold is
// rejected, one tick outside rests.
//
//   Order book   from GET /api/exchange/orderbook/:pair
//     buy   <  best ask
//     sell  >  best bid
//
//   AMM pool     from GET /api/exchange/pool/:pair
//     let B = reserveBase, Q = reserveQuote, f = feeRate
//     buy   <  Q / (B * (1 - f))
//     sell  >  Q * (1 - f) / B
//
// Worked example using the live NEOX_USDC pool above
// (B = 8202353.6634527, Q = 636.94745563, f = 0.003):
//   pool ask = Q / (B * 0.997) = 0.00007788789340  -> buy must be BELOW this
//   pool bid = Q * 0.997 / B   = 0.00007742126703  -> sell must be ABOVE this
//
// ROUNDING: the threshold rarely lands on the pair's pricePrecision, so round
// the right way or the rounding alone will get you rejected. Round a BUY price
// DOWN and a SELL price UP. Here, at pricePrecision 8, a buy rounded to
// 0.00007789 is ABOVE the true ask and is refused; 0.00007788 rests.
//
// WHY THE POOL MATTERS MORE THAN THE BOOK: the pool charges 0.30%, which is
// higher than the 0.20% taker fee, so crossing it is the more expensive
// mistake. That 0.30% is taken inside the swap arithmetic and does NOT appear
// in the taker_fee or maker_fee field of the resulting trade: both read 0 on
// an AMM fill. Do not reconcile pool costs from those fields.
//
// Being FILLED as a maker later is normal and is what post-only is for. The
// rejection only ever happens at placement.

